*1 [[Calamary]] spawns as the boss after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*1 [[Elizabeth the LVIth]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
A very underwhelming level. If you have all six sets of [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] from [[Into the Future]], the Elizabeths will only have 600,000 health and 2,500 attack power. Sync them and unleash [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]], who will land 7 hits (595,000). Then have [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] take off the rest of their health; past that point, Calamary on her own will not be a threat. You can use [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Rover Cat Mk II]] as a meatshield if it's sufficiently leveled, preferably level 30 or higher, but even [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall/Manic Eraser Cat]] and [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] can already do an adequate job at tanking the Elizabeths.

Alternatively, if one were to use Manic Eraser, Rover Cat Mk II and [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] to stall the Elizabeths and push them behind the base, one can use Awakened Bahamut and other [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]] to cheese the stage, as the Elizabeths will stack up and fill the enemy limit, preventing Calamary from spawning.

If one is doing this stage on 4 Crown, Talented [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Dancer Cat]] can make this stage extremely easy, as Dancer is immune to weaken and, if talented, waves.

==Trivia==
*Since its Japanese name is Iberico Plains, this stage's main threat being [[Elizabeth the LVIth]] may be a reference to [[wikipedia:Jamón ibérico|''jamón ibérico'']], a variety of cured pork made from [[wikipedia:Black Iberian pig|black Iberian pigs]] in Spain and Portugal.

